module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ULiftUnit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.CoherentKernelOnSite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.QuasicoherentFromCoherence
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.RingedSite

/-!
# Multiples of a sheaf of modules by an ideal of a base ring

Let `X` be a ringed site whose structure sheaf receives a compatible family of ring maps from a
fixed ring `A`, and let `F` be a sheaf of modules on `X`. For an ideal `I` of `A` the subsheaf
`I F` of `F` is the least subsheaf which, over every object, contains the products of the
sections of `F` with the image of `I`. This file constructs that subsheaf, proves that it is of
finite type when `I` is finitely generated and `F` is of finite type, and deduces that it is
coherent, hence quasi-coherent, when `F` is coherent.

Finiteness is what the base ring buys: the generators of `I` give *global* scalars, so a local
generating family of `F` multiplies into a local generating family of `I F` on the very same
covering, with no second covering to intersect. The engine is therefore stated for a compatible
family of finitely many global scalars, and the ideal statement is its corollary.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.scalarMultiples`: the submodule of the underlying presheaf of
  `F` spanned over each object by the products of the sections with a finite compatible family
  of scalars.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.scalarMultiplesSubsheaf`: its local closure, the least subsheaf
  of `F` containing it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.baseIdealMultiple`: the subsheaf `I F` attached to an ideal `I`
  of the base ring.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.le_localClosure` and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localClosure_le`: the
  universal property of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localClosure`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.baseIdealMultiple_le_iff`: the universal property of `I F`,
  tested object by object on the products.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.scalarMultiplesSubsheaf_isFiniteType` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.baseIdealMultiple_isFiniteType`: finiteness.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.baseIdealMultiple_isCoherentOnSite`: `I F` is coherent when `F`
  is, which is Stacks 01BY (1) applied to the inclusion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.baseIdealMultiple_isQuasicoherentOnSite`: `I F` is
  quasi-coherent when `F` is coherent.

## Implementation notes

The subsheaf is an infimum of subsheaves rather than a sectionwise image, so it exists with no
finiteness hypothesis on `I` and needs no sheafification; finiteness enters only in the
theorems. When `I` is finitely generated the infimum is identified with the local closure of the
presheaf submodule of products, which is the form the finite-type argument uses.

The ring of scalars is spelled `X.ringSheaf.obj.obj U` everywhere, never `X.O.obj.obj U`: the
module structure on the sections of `F` is declared at the first spelling and commutativity at
the second, and mixing them leaves a `Module` instance that is only found by relaxing
transparency. `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.ringSheaf_isMulCommutative` transports the
commutativity to the first spelling once and for all, as the mixin `IsMulCommutative`, whose
`mul_comm'` is what the one commutation step of the finite-type proof uses.

For the same reason restriction of sections is written with `PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ` and
not with `PresheafOfModules.map`: the first has the plain module of sections as its codomain,
the second a `ModuleCat.restrictScalars` of it, and a membership statement written with the
second fixes the ambient module at a spelling that the next rewrite no longer type-checks
against.

`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPowerProduct` is the companion construction for a *sheaf* of
ideals on the site. The two agree when the sheaf of ideals is the one generated by the image of
`I`, but neither is stated in terms of the other: the global generators that make the finiteness
argument here work have no counterpart there.

Coherence of a submodule of a coherent sheaf is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherentOnSite_of_injective` and quasi-coherence of a coherent sheaf is
`SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isCoherentOnSite`; the latter is stated with the module
universe equal to the ring universe, which is why the quasi-coherence statement is the only one
below not proved at independent universes.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe u v w m

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

section LocalClosure

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}
  {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{m} R}

/-- A submodule of the underlying presheaf of a sheaf of modules is contained in its local
closure. -/
theorem le_localClosure (N : M.val.Submodule) : N ≤ (localClosure M N).toSubmodule :=
  fun U _ hx => N.toSubfunctor.le_sheafify J U hx

/-- The local closure is the least submodule of the *sheaf* containing a given submodule of its
underlying presheaf: a section lying locally in `N` lies in any subsheaf containing `N`. -/
theorem localClosure_le {N : M.val.Submodule} {P : M.Submodule} (h : N ≤ P.toSubmodule) :
    localClosure M N ≤ P := by
  intro U x hx
  exact P.isSheaf x (J.superset_covering (fun V f hf => h (op V) hf) hx)

end LocalClosure

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

open PresheafOfModules Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-- The ring of sections of the structure sheaf of a ringed site is commutative, at the spelling
`X.ringSheaf.obj.obj U` in which the sections of a sheaf of modules are a module over it. -/
instance ringSheaf_isMulCommutative (X : RingedSite.{u, v, w}) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    IsMulCommutative ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj U) :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsMulCommutative (X.O.obj.obj U))

/-! ### The subsheaf generated by a compatible family of global scalars -/

section ScalarMultiples

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, v, w})
  (F : SheafOfModules.{m} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) {k : ℕ}
  (b : ∀ U : X.Cᵒᵖ, Fin k → (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj U)
  (hb : ∀ {U V : X.Cᵒᵖ} (f : U ⟶ V) (i : Fin k),
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.map f (b U i) = b V i)

/-- The submodule of the underlying presheaf of `F` spanned over each object by the products of
the sections of `F` with a finite family of scalars compatible with restriction. The spanning
set is itself stable under restriction, which is what makes the family of spans a presheaf
submodule. -/
def scalarMultiples : F.val.Submodule where
  obj U := Submodule.span ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj U)
    (Set.range (fun p : Fin k × F.val.obj U => b U p.1 • p.2))
  map {U V} f := by
    apply Submodule.span_le.mpr
    rintro _ ⟨⟨i, x⟩, rfl⟩
    change F.val.map f (b U i • x) ∈
      Submodule.span ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj V)
        (Set.range (fun p : Fin k × F.val.obj V => b V p.1 • p.2))
    rw [F.val.map_smul]
    change (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.map f (b U i) • F.val.map f x ∈ _
    rw [hb]
    exact Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self (i, F.val.map f x))

/-- The least subsheaf of `F` containing the products of its sections with a compatible family
of global scalars. -/
def scalarMultiplesSubsheaf : F.Submodule := localClosure F (scalarMultiples X F b hb)

/-- When the family of scalars is the image of a finite generating family of an ideal `I` of a
base ring, the products span the extension of `I` times the whole module. -/
theorem scalarMultiples_obj_eq (A : Type*) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (f : ∀ U : X.Cᵒᵖ, A →+* (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj U) (a : Fin k → A)
    (ha : Ideal.span (Set.range a) = I) (hab : ∀ U i, f U (a i) = b U i) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    (scalarMultiples X F b hb).obj U =
      Ideal.map (f U) I •
        (⊤ : Submodule ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj U) (F.val.obj U)) := by
  have hmap : Ideal.map (f U) I = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => f U (a i)) := by
    rw [← ha, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
    rfl
  apply le_antisymm
  · refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨⟨i, y⟩, rfl⟩
    refine Submodule.smul_mem_smul ?_ Submodule.mem_top
    rw [hmap, ← hab U i]
    exact Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self i)
  · refine Submodule.smul_le.mpr ?_
    intro r hr y _
    rw [hmap] at hr
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := (Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun _).mp hr
    rw [← hc, Finset.sum_smul]
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => ?_
    rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_smul, hab U i]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self (i, y)))

/-- The submodule of the underlying presheaf spanned by a family of global sections. It is the
construction `Stacks.SheafOfModules.spanSubmodule` at a module universe independent of the ring
universe, which is the generality the finite-type proof below is carried out in. -/
private def sectionsSpan {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
    {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}} (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) {ι : Type*} (g : ι → M.sections) :
    M.val.Submodule where
  obj U := Submodule.span (R.obj.obj U) (Set.range (fun i => (g i).eval U))
  map {U V} f := by
    apply Submodule.span_le.mpr
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    change M.val.map f ((g i).eval U) ∈
      Submodule.span (R.obj.obj V) (Set.range (fun i => (g i).eval V))
    rw [show M.val.map f ((g i).eval U) = (g i).eval V from (g i).property f]
    exact Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self i)

/-- **The subsheaf generated by finitely many global scalars is of finite type when the module
is.** A local generating family `g` of `F` over an object multiplies into the family of products
`bᵢ · gⱼ`, which generates the subsheaf over the same object: a section of the subsheaf lies
locally in the span of the products `bᵢ · x`, and each such `x` is in turn locally a combination
of the `gⱼ`, so two successive coverings — composed here by passing through the local closure on
the slice site — exhibit it as a combination of the `bᵢ · gⱼ`. -/
theorem scalarMultiplesSubsheaf_isFiniteType (hF : IsFiniteType X.J F.val) :
    IsFiniteType X.J (scalarMultiplesSubsheaf X F b hb).toSheafOfModules.val := by
  classical
  let P := scalarMultiples X F b hb
  let N := scalarMultiplesSubsheaf X F b hb
  let M := N.toSheafOfModules
  obtain ⟨I, U, hU, hg⟩ := hF.exists_generators
  refine ⟨I, U, hU, ?_⟩
  intro i
  obtain ⟨l, g, hg⟩ := hg i
  let e : Fin k × Fin l ≃ Fin (k * l) := finProdFinEquiv
  let gN : Fin (k * l) → M.val.obj (op (U i)) := fun j =>
    ⟨b (op (U i)) (e.symm j).1 • g (e.symm j).2,
      le_localClosure P _ (Submodule.subset_span
        (Set.mem_range_self ((e.symm j).1, g (e.symm j).2)))⟩
  refine ⟨k * l, gN, ?_⟩
  let gF : Fin (k * l) → (F.over (U i)).sections := fun j =>
    SheafOfModules.sectionOver F (gN j).val
  let Q := localClosure (F.over (U i)) (sectionsSpan (F.over (U i)) gF)
  have hPQ (V : X.C) (f : V ⟶ U i) :
      P.obj (op V) ≤ Q.toSubmodule.obj (op (Over.mk f)) := by
    apply Submodule.span_le.mpr
    rintro _ ⟨⟨a, x⟩, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨S, hS, hs⟩ := hg V f x
    apply Q.isSheaf (X := op (Over.mk f)) (b (op V) a • x)
    apply (X.J.over (U i)).superset_covering _
      (X.J.overEquiv_symm_mem_over (Over.mk f) S hS)
    intro W h hh
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hs W.left h.left ((Sieve.overEquiv_symm_iff S h).mp hh)
    apply le_localClosure (sectionsSpan (F.over (U i)) gF)
    change (F.val.restrictₛₗ h.left.op (b (op V) a • x) : F.val.obj (op W.left)) ∈
      Submodule.span ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj (op W.left))
        (Set.range (fun j => (F.val.restrictₛₗ W.hom.op (gN j).val : F.val.obj (op W.left))))
    rw [map_smulₛₗ,
      show ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.map h.left.op) (b (op V) a) =
        b (op W.left) a from hb h.left.op a,
      ← hc, Finset.smul_sum]
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun j _ => ?_
    rw [← mul_smul, mul_comm' (b (op W.left) a) (c j), mul_smul]
    refine Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ?_
    have hw : W.hom = h.left ≫ f := (Over.w h).symm
    have he : (F.val.restrictₛₗ W.hom.op (gN (e (a, j))).val : F.val.obj (op W.left)) =
        b (op W.left) a • F.val.restrictₛₗ (h.left ≫ f).op (g j) := by
      change (F.val.restrictₛₗ W.hom.op
        (b (op (U i)) (e.symm (e (a, j))).1 • g (e.symm (e (a, j))).2) :
          F.val.obj (op W.left)) = _
      rw [Equiv.symm_apply_apply, map_smulₛₗ, hb, hw]
    exact he ▸ Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self (e (a, j)))
  intro V f x
  have hx : x.val ∈ Q.toSubmodule.obj (op (Over.mk f)) := by
    apply Q.isSheaf (X := op (Over.mk f)) x.val
    apply (X.J.over (U i)).superset_covering _
      (X.J.overEquiv_symm_mem_over (Over.mk f) (P.toSubfunctor.sieveOfSection x.val)
        x.property)
    exact fun W _ hh => hPQ W.left W.hom hh
  change (sectionsSpan (F.over (U i)) gF).toSubfunctor.sieveOfSection
      (U := op (Over.mk f)) x.val ∈ X.J.over (U i) (Over.mk f) at hx
  let S := (sectionsSpan (F.over (U i)) gF).toSubfunctor.sieveOfSection
      (U := op (Over.mk f)) x.val
  refine ⟨Sieve.overEquiv (Over.mk f) S, (X.J.mem_over_iff S).mp hx, ?_⟩
  intro W h hh
  have hh' : S (Over.homMk h : Over.mk (h ≫ f) ⟶ Over.mk f) :=
    (Sieve.overEquiv_iff S h).mp hh
  replace hh' : (F.val.restrictₛₗ h.op x.val : F.val.obj (op W)) ∈
    Submodule.span ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj (op W))
      (Set.range (fun j => (F.val.restrictₛₗ (h ≫ f).op (gN j).val : F.val.obj (op W)))) := hh'
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := (Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun _).mp hh'
  exact ⟨a, Subtype.ext (Eq.trans (map_sum (N.toSubmodule.obj (op W)).subtype _ Finset.univ) ha)⟩

end ScalarMultiples

/-! ### The multiple of a module by an ideal of a base ring -/

section BaseIdeal

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, v, w})
  (F : SheafOfModules.{m} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
  (A : Type*) [CommRing A]
  (φ : ∀ U : X.Cᵒᵖ, A →+* (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj U) (I : Ideal A)

/-- The subsheaf `I F` of `F` cut out by an ideal `I` of a base ring mapping compatibly into the
structure sheaf: the least subsheaf containing, over every object, the products of the sections
of `F` with the extension of `I` there. -/
def baseIdealMultiple : F.Submodule :=
  sInf { N : F.Submodule | ∀ U : X.Cᵒᵖ,
    Ideal.map (φ U) I •
        (⊤ : Submodule ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj U) (F.val.obj U)) ≤
      N.toSubmodule.obj U }

/-- **The universal property of `I F`.** A subsheaf of `F` contains `I F` exactly when it
contains the products of the sections with the extension of `I` over every object. -/
theorem baseIdealMultiple_le_iff (N : F.Submodule) :
    baseIdealMultiple X F A φ I ≤ N ↔ ∀ U : X.Cᵒᵖ,
      Ideal.map (φ U) I •
          (⊤ : Submodule ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj U) (F.val.obj U)) ≤
        N.toSubmodule.obj U := by
  constructor
  · intro h U
    refine le_trans ?_ (h U)
    change _ ≤ (baseIdealMultiple X F A φ I).toSubmodule.obj U
    simp only [baseIdealMultiple, SheafOfModules.Submodule.toSubmodule_sInf,
      PresheafOfModules.Submodule.sInf_obj]
    refine le_iInf₂ fun K hK => ?_
    obtain ⟨K', hK', rfl⟩ := hK
    exact hK' U
  · exact fun h => sInf_le h

variable {k : ℕ}

/-- With a finite generating family of `I` to hand, `I F` is the local closure of the presheaf
submodule of products with the images of the generators. -/
theorem baseIdealMultiple_eq_scalarMultiplesSubsheaf
    (hφ : ∀ {U V : X.Cᵒᵖ} (f : U ⟶ V) (x : A),
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.map f (φ U x) = φ V x)
    (a : Fin k → A) (ha : Ideal.span (Set.range a) = I) :
    baseIdealMultiple X F A φ I =
      scalarMultiplesSubsheaf X F (fun U i => φ U (a i)) (fun f i => hφ f (a i)) := by
  have hobj := scalarMultiples_obj_eq X F (fun U i => φ U (a i)) (fun f i => hφ f (a i))
    A I φ a ha (fun _ _ => rfl)
  apply le_antisymm
  · refine (baseIdealMultiple_le_iff X F A φ I _).mpr fun U => ?_
    rw [← hobj U]
    exact le_localClosure _ U
  · refine localClosure_le fun U => ?_
    rw [hobj U]
    exact (baseIdealMultiple_le_iff X F A φ I _).mp le_rfl U

/-- **`I F` is of finite type when `I` is finitely generated and `F` is of finite type.** -/
theorem baseIdealMultiple_isFiniteType
    (hφ : ∀ {U V : X.Cᵒᵖ} (f : U ⟶ V) (x : A),
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.map f (φ U x) = φ V x)
    (hI : I.FG) (hF : IsFiniteType X.J F.val) :
    IsFiniteType X.J (baseIdealMultiple X F A φ I).toSheafOfModules.val := by
  obtain ⟨n, a, ha⟩ := Submodule.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family.mp hI
  rw [baseIdealMultiple_eq_scalarMultiplesSubsheaf X F A φ I hφ a ha]
  exact scalarMultiplesSubsheaf_isFiniteType X F _ _ hF

/-- **`I F` is coherent when `F` is**, for `I` finitely generated: it is of finite type and a
subobject of `F`, so Stacks 01BY (1) applies. -/
theorem baseIdealMultiple_isCoherentOnSite
    (hφ : ∀ {U V : X.Cᵒᵖ} (f : U ⟶ V) (x : A),
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.map f (φ U x) = φ V x)
    (hI : I.FG) (hF : SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite F) :
    SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite (baseIdealMultiple X F A φ I).toSheafOfModules :=
  isCoherentOnSite_of_injective (baseIdealMultiple X F A φ I).ι
    (injective_val_of_mono (baseIdealMultiple X F A φ I).ι)
    (baseIdealMultiple_isFiniteType X F A φ I hφ hI hF.isFiniteType) hF

end BaseIdeal

/-- **`I F` is quasi-coherent when `F` is coherent**, for `I` finitely generated: it is coherent
by `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.baseIdealMultiple_isCoherentOnSite`, and a coherent sheaf of
modules on a site is quasi-coherent. -/
theorem baseIdealMultiple_isQuasicoherentOnSite (X : RingedSite.{u, v, w})
    (F : SheafOfModules.{w} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) (A : Type*) [CommRing A]
    (φ : ∀ U : X.Cᵒᵖ, A →+* (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.obj U) (I : Ideal A)
    (hφ : ∀ {U V : X.Cᵒᵖ} (f : U ⟶ V) (x : A),
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O).obj.map f (φ U x) = φ V x)
    (hI : I.FG) (hF : SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite F) :
    (baseIdealMultiple X F A φ I).toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite :=
  let := baseIdealMultiple_isCoherentOnSite X F A φ I hφ hI hF
  inferInstance

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
